# Docker build context is the repo ROOT (the civfix-infra compose sets build.context to this checkout).
# Keep the context small + reproducible: never ship host node_modules / build outputs / secrets into
# the build. The Dockerfiles install + build fresh INSIDE the linux image so native binaries (sharp,
# ffmpeg-static, ffprobe-static) are fetched for the target platform, not copied from the host.

# Dependencies + build outputs (re-created in the image)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage

# VCS + CI + editor cruft
.git
.gitignore
.github
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Local env / secrets (the container gets config via env_file at run time, NOT baked into the image)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Docker + compose meta (not needed inside the build)
**/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore

# Deploy/infra lives in the civfix-infra repo now; the only thing left here is the email-worker
# (a standalone Cloudflare Worker) which must never be baked into the api/worker image.
infra

# Tests + fixtures are not needed for a production image build (build stage only runs tsup, not tests)
**/test
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/vitest.config.ts

# Drizzle generated inspection output (the canonical hand SQL in services/api/drizzle/*.sql is kept)
**/drizzle/_generated
